{"type":"message","id":"eeac67df","parentId":"634d2b0d","timestamp":"2026-03-13T18:17:48.611Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\nGot it, let's tackle this task step by step. First, I need to go to the target directory: /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace/projects/daily-news-crawler. Then I need to search for all configuration files there, right? Common config file extensions are yaml, yml, json, toml, env, conf, config etc. But first, let's check what files are in that directory first, then search for content that has government URLs, specifically looking for files that have the 17 government site URLs list.\n\nWait first, let's run a command to list all files in that directory, then grep for files that contain government URLs? Or better, use find to get all config files, then search their content. Let's first execute a find command to get all config files in that directory, then search for the URL content.\n\nWait the task says search all files that contain the 17 government website URL list. So let's first run:\ncd /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace/projects/daily-news-crawler && find . -type f \\( -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" -o -name \"*.json\" -o -name \"*.toml\" -o -name \"*.env\" -o -name \"*.conf\" -o -name \"*.config\" \\) | xargs grep -l \"gov.cn\" 2>/dev/null\nThat should find all config files that have gov.cn URLs, which are government sites. Then once we get those file paths, we can read each of them to get the content.\n\nWait but first let's run that exec command to find the relevant files. Let's do that.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_qzykmj0ym4ytw95fpfymb1yn","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace/projects/daily-news-crawler && find . -type f \\( -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" -o -name \"*.json\" -o -name \"*.toml\" -o -name \"*.env\" -o -name \"*.conf\" -o -name \"*.config\" \\) | xargs grep -l \"gov.cn\" 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"volces-com","model":"ark-code-latest","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773425863744}}
